te-coverage.test.ts. The agent must not create it (or if it does, it gets overwritten). Hmm, actually \"frozenTestsUnchanged\": true — the grader checks that the frozen tests are unchanged.\n\nActually let me re-read: \"hiddenTestPaths\" = list of tests that are hidden from the agent (they'll be applied at grading). The agent's job is to make the repo state such that these hidden tests pass. But the agent doesn't see them.\n\nBut wait — \"Do not inspect or modify tests in the final hidden oracle.\" So the hidden test files are given at grade time.\n\nHmm, but which files does the grader supply? Let me think about what the agent must do:\n1. Restore the missing pre-existing guard test files (which are in `base`)? Actually no — the `base` dir is the base commit snapshot. The agent dir is a fresh `git archive` of base commit but with those files deleted? Let me check: the diff showed base has 8 files that agent lacks. That's suspicious: the task says \"移除树中不存在的 ... 引用\" (remove references to files not in tree). So it seems the agent tree deliberately has those files removed, and the agent must ADD them back... Hmm.\n\nWait, actually maybe not. Let me re-read: the tasks are \"regression\" kind, i.e., the agent is given a repo state where the task's solution was reverted in some way. The agent must re-implement it.\n\nLet me look at the manifest more carefully to understand the setup. Let me check the \"oracle.commandLines\" and the input digests. The inputDigests include hashes for harness-gap-a05-...-reverify.md, tests/unit/resource-aware-wave-scheduler.test.ts, performance-budgets.test.ts, deprecation-counters.test.ts, .../deprecation-counters.test.ts, compaction-budget-shadow.test.ts, compression-planner.test.ts, context-orchestrator.test.ts, compaction-promotion.test.ts, a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts.\n\nThese \"inputDigests\" are the expected SHA256 of the *reference solution's* versions of those files. So the grader checks that the repo state matches? Not exactly —