{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"reasoning","text":"Interesting. `base` has most pre-existing tests matching the reference input digests, except:\n- tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts: expected 4502f116..., base has a27fb409...\n- openclaw_runtime/src/context-engine/context-orchestrator.test.ts: expected 40b9500b..., base has 8a9f1c84...\n\nHmm, so base differs. Actually wait — the reference digests are for the *reference solution* (commit 47388bf...) state maybe. Let me think.\n\nActually the inputDigests in the oracle are for the *task input* files, i.e., the state at baseCommit fd04f0b4... But maybe the digests were computed at the reference revision. Hmm, \"inputDigests\" typically means the digest of the input file expected (to detect tests modified). Hmm.\n\nInteresting: performance-budgets and context-orchestrator differ between base and the expected digest. But actually the missing files in agent: this is an \"isolated repository task\" where the agent workspace had the A5 tests removed? Wait no.\n\nActually let's reconsider. The `agent` workspace is the trial starting point. The \"base\" directory contains... hmm. Both base and agent are near-identical (17524 vs 17518 files) with base having 8 extra files that agent lacks. But those 8 files are exactly the A5-related pre-existing tests + reference tests. Wait no, agent lacks 8 files: performance-budgets, deprecation-counters (tests/unit), resource-aware-wave-scheduler (tests/unit), and 5 openclaw_runtime test files.\n\nHold on — that's odd for a \"baseline\" trial. The task says implement the change. The baseline arm presumably starts from a state where these files are absent, and the agent must create them.\n\nHmm wait. Actually, let me reconsider: maybe `base` is the reference/base commit snapshot given for comparison — it's a full checkout at baseCommit fd04f0b4. And `agent` is the same but with the 8 test files deleted (tasks removed them since they're \"hidden oracle\" tests?