esume` resume 后重跑：`openclaw_runtime/src/agents/cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` 实现 + `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts`（3.6）+ `tests/unit/deep/a5-deep.test.ts`，PASS。\" So the reference implemented cross-area-facades.ts and cross-area-composition.test.ts.\n\nCriterion 8: \"移除树中不存在的 tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts 与 cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts 引用；requiredTests 与 coverage 守卫同步。\" — \"remove references in the tree to the nonexistent ...\" Possibly means: remove stale references to these paths *from places that assert they don't exist*, OR it means the tree previously had references to them assuming they exist... Ugh.\n\nHmm, maybe the truth: The base tree (fd04f0b4) does NOT have cross-area-facades.ts. The a4 spec pattern: A04 fixed spec drift by adding real tests. For A05, maybe the historical solution DID add cross-area-facades.ts and cross-area-composition.test.ts as new files (restoring what area-composition-spec.md specifies). Then criterion 8's \"移除树中不存在的引用\" refers to removing those paths from the `source-inventory.json` \"missingLegacyPaths\" list? Or removing references from other specs?\n\nLet me search the tree for references to 'cross-area-composition' and 'cross-area-facades'.\n\nLet me do that now. Also search for 'replanOnResume'.\n\nLet me get more info before deciding.\n\nAlso: since other trials exist in `trials/`, but the sibling trial dirs for tf-0297-a05 (baseline-2, -3, treatment-*) may be present. Let me check.\n\nActually, an important realization: The `base` dir likely represents the state of the repo at the *solution* revision for reference (no—). Hmm, base has 8 test files that agent lacks, and agent lacks them intentionally. So base = full repo at baseCommit? But then agent = base minus 8 files. Why would the harness remove them? Because those are the \"hidden\" tests the agent must recreate? That's a weird mechanic but plausible for a \"reverify gate\" task where the deliverable is tests.\n\nHmm, actually maybe not r