den tests including `tests/unit/a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts`.\n\nBut `tests/unit/a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts` is in the targetScope — and it's a hidden signal path. Since it's hidden, the agent shouldn't write it (it would be overwritten). But the acceptance criterion 8 says \"移除树中不存在的 tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts 与 cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts 引用；requiredTests 与 coverage 守卫同步.\"\n\nHmm. Let's carefully figure out what's needed for the oracle to pass. The oracle command:\n1. `pnpm exec vitest run tests/unit/resource-aware-wave-scheduler.test.ts tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts tests/unit/a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`\n2. `pnpm --dir openclaw_runtime exec node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts src/agents/agent-hooks/compaction-budget-shadow.test.ts packages/agent-core/src/harness/compaction/compression-planner.test.ts src/context-engine/context-orchestrator.test.ts src/agents/agent-hooks/compaction-promotion.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`\n\nThe hidden tests are the guard tests. But the preexisting guard paths (`tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts`, `performance-budgets.test.ts`, `resource-aware-wave-scheduler.test.ts`, and the runtime ones) exist in `base` but are missing in `agent`. Are they \"hidden\"? They're listed in the manifest's `hiddenTestPaths`. So yes, the harness removed them from the agent workspace and the grader will restore them from the reference.\n\nHmm, but that would mean the agent can't verify anything. That can't be right for a \"baseline\" arm... Actually wait: this is a *baseline* arm trial where the agent is just given the task and must produce a correct final state. The hidden tests are restored at grading time.\n\nHmm, but acceptance criteria mention specific test files with p99, etc. Also `inputDigests` includes `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts` with `bf5559f7...` which matches the `base` copy EXACTLY. And `tests/un