eate the new spec `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a05-adaptive-context-budget-pilot-reverify.md`.\n4. Create docs: `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a05-adaptive-context-budget-gate.md`, `a05-acceptance.json`, `A05-SHA256SUMS`.\n5. Possibly create `openclaw_runtime/src/agents/cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts`, `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts`, `tests/unit/deep/a5-deep.test.ts`? But the guard says frontmatter must NOT contain those refs. Hmm, criterion 8 says \"移除树中不存在的 cross-area-composition.test.ts 与 cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts 引用\" — remove references to files that DON'T exist in the tree. That means: in the reference solution, those files do NOT exist, and references to them must be removed from the spec (requiredTests).\n\nBut criterion 3 says the implementation + cross-area-composition test + a5-deep test PASS... \n\nHmm, that's contradictory unless criterion 3 refers to test *coverage* that is currently satisfied by OTHER tests (e.g., resource-aware-wave-scheduler covers wave immutability, and the \"resume re-plan\" is covered elsewhere). Let me reconsider: acceptanceCriteria in TASK.json are probably the *reference* description of what was done:\n\n\"判据3 `ContextBudgetPlanner.replanOnResume` resume 后重跑：`openclaw_runtime/src/agents/cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` 实现 + `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts`（3.6）+ `tests/unit/deep/a5-deep.test.ts`，PASS。\"\n\nand \n\n\"移除树中不存在的 `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` 与 `cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` 引用；requiredTests 与 coverage 守卫同步。\"\n\nHmm, \"移除树中不存在的 X 引用\" = remove references (in the spec) to X which doesn't exist in the tree. So the reference solution did NOT create those; it removed the stale references. And criterion 3... maybe reworded: the ContextBudgetPlanner replanOnResume is implemented in cross-area-facades.ts... \n\nThis is confusing. Two readings. Let me look at the actual targetScope: it lists both `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` and doesn't list `openclaw_r