ain `degrade_to_default_budget`\n- scheduler contains the wave-immutability text\n- perf contains p99 and spec contains \"p99 ≤ 30ms\" and \"300ms\"\n- maybe spec contains something about resume re-plan residual\n\nGiven A02's guard explicitly asserts the frontmatter must NOT contain `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` and `cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts`, and criterion 8 for A05 says the same thing about the same two paths — I'm now fairly confident the A05 guard does the same: **frontmatter must not contain those two paths**. So:\n\n- Do NOT create `cross-area-facades.ts` / `cross-area-composition.test.ts` (or if created, they must not be referenced in frontmatter — but creating them isn't needed).\n- Remove those two lines from the a5 spec frontmatter.\n\nHmm, but should I create them? If the guard checks `expect(frontmatter).not.toContain(...)`, creating the files is harmless for that check but then requiredTests wouldn't include them. But if the guard instead checks `expect(existsSync(...)).toBe(true)` for those paths... conflict. A02's precedent tips me to \"not contained\".\n\nHmm, but criterion 3 requires `ContextBudgetPlanner.replanOnResume` implemented. If guard checks that, I need the implementation. Where would the guard find it? Possibly in the scheduler? Let me look at `resource-aware-wave-scheduler.ts` and its restored test to see if there's already a re-plan/resume surface.\n\nLet me now actually read files. Enough speculation.\n\nLet me read:\n- openclaw_runtime/src/agents/resource-aware-wave-scheduler.ts\n- docs/runtime-design/area-composition-spec.md (pair 5 section)\n- docs/runtime-design/area-5-adaptive-context-budget.md\n- harness/specs/tasks/a2-multi-agent-orchestration-pilot.md (to see how the stale refs were removed + requiredTests final content)\n- base/tests/unit/resource-aware-wave-scheduler.test.ts (the restored one)\n- base/tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts\n- base/tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\n\nLet me batch t