t.ts` reference from requiredTests.\n\nHmm, but criterion 3 explicitly lists cross-area-composition.test.ts.\n\nHmm hold on, let me recheck: is `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` in `targetScope`? Yes:\n```\n\"tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts\",\n```\nAnd the manifest `missingLegacyPaths` includes it and cross-area-facades.ts.\n\nHmm, and the reference solution's `testPaths` does NOT include cross-area-composition.test.ts. So the reference did NOT create it. The reference created `cross-area-facades.ts` though? Let me check by looking at the reference workspace.\n\nI don't have the A05 reference workspace... but `_a01verify` has cross-area-facades.ts. So cross-area-facades.ts is a real file in the family of reference solutions.\n\nHmm, wait. Let me reconsider: maybe `_a01verify` is actually the A01 *vendor baseline* tree that already includes all A0x packet results (the \"treatment\" environment). Since A01's re-verify depends on the shared bits.\n\nActually — hmm, let's test: does `_a01verify/ClawX` contain `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts`, `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-acceptance.json`?\n\nLet me just check comprehensively."}}
