{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_191","type":"reasoning","text":"So at the candidate commit 96afc2c, the frozen files exist. The trial's agent workspace has these files *removed* (they were scrubbed as oracle tests). Wait — actually the manifest says `hiddenTestPaths` are restored at grading time. Let me understand: hidden tests are removed from the agent workspace and restored by the grader before running. So the agent must NOT create them. And the agent's implementation (production source) must make those hidden tests pass.\n\nKey insight: `openclaw_runtime/src/agents/cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` — is it a hidden test path? No, it's a source file. But in the agent workspace it's absent while in `base` it's absent too... wait, let me check: in the agent workspace `openclaw_runtime/src/agents/cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` is absent. In base also absent. Hmm, but the reference commit 47388bf has it present? Let me check.\n\nActually earlier: `base False | agent False | openclaw_runtime/src/agents/cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts`. So it's absent in base too. And the reference solution (47388bf, \"restore stale paths\") - let me check if cross-area-facades.ts was added by that commit.\n\nThe diff stat showed 47388bf touched only 4 files:\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a05-adaptive-context-budget-gate.md\n- harness/specs/tasks/a5-adaptive-context-budget-pilot.md\n- harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a05-adaptive-context-budget-pilot-reverify.md\n- tests/unit/a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts\n\nSo cross-area-facades.ts already existed at the *reference* commit per 96afc2c having it. But the reference commit for this task is 47388bf whose base is fd04f0b. Let me check what exists at 47388bf vs fd04f0b for cross-area-facades.ts.\n\nWait, the manifest says referenceCommit 47388bf, baseCommit fd04f0b. But the inputDigests show the *frozen oracle tests* (as they will be restored at grading). These include:\n- tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts (absent in