r this run has `hiddenTestPaths` (global) — a list of many test paths. For A05 the relevant sealed ones are in inputDigests. cross-area-composition.test.ts and a5-deep.test.ts are NOT sealed → I must create them (they're in hiddenTestPaths? Let me check the global hiddenTestPaths list I saw):\n```\n\"tests/unit/a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts\",\n...\n```\nThe hiddenTestPaths list included performance-budgets, deprecation-counters, a01..a06 guards, resource-aware-wave-scheduler, runtime deprecation-counters, anomaly-classifier, decision-quality-auditor, a4-deep, trace-truncation, a04 guard, compaction-budget-shadow, compression-planner, context-orchestrator, compaction-promotion, a05 guard, file-fingerprint, runtime-resume-shadow, long-task-checkpoint-builder, long-task-control, a06 guard.\n\nNote: cross-area-composition.test.ts and deep/a5-deep.test.ts are NOT in hiddenTestPaths! Because they are NON-sealed tests that the agent must author (and they're generic to A5, not sealed oracles). Wait but then why did the agent workspace not have them? Because they don't exist at baseCommit fd04f0b4 — they were added later by 65005caf4 (TF-0264 restore). Hmm, so the agent workspace base is f0040b (which lacks them), and the sealed stuff...\n\nUgh, I'm overcomplicating. Let me just directly compare the agent workspace to 96afc2c and to fd04f0b4 to see which it matches.\n\nLet me do that now."}}
