STS check requires they exist with specific content.\n\nWait, but \"hiddenTestPaths\" includes cross-area-composition.test.ts? Let me check: hiddenTestPaths list (global) includes \"tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts\", \"tests/unit/resource-aware-wave-scheduler.test.ts\", \"openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts\", ..., \"openclaw_runtime/src/context-engine/context-orchestrator.test.ts\", \"openclaw_runtime/src/agents/agent-hooks/compaction-promotion.test.ts\", \"tests/unit/a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts\". Hmm, cross-area-composition.test.ts is NOT in the hiddenTestPaths global list. And deep/a5-deep.test.ts is NOT either. Let me double-check.\n\nLooking at the hiddenTestPaths list... it contains a4-deep, a3-deep? Let me look: \"tests/unit/decision-quality-auditor.test.ts\", \"tests/unit/deep/a4-deep.test.ts\", ... Actually I see \"tests/unit/deep/a4-deep.test.ts\" but not a5-deep. And \"tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts\" is not present.\n\nSo: agent must create `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts`, `tests/unit/deep/a5-deep.test.ts`, and `openclaw_runtime/src/agents/cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts`.\n\nAnd the oracle command runs:\n`pnpm exec vitest run tests/unit/resource-aware-wave-scheduler.test.ts tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts tests/unit/a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`\n\nHmm — that only runs 4 test files. cross-area-composition and a5-deep are NOT run by the oracle. So they only need to EXIST and contain the pinned strings (checked by the hidden guard's readFileSync).\n\nAlso performance-budgets.test.ts (oracle version) imports FrameworkIn from cross-area-facades: `ContextBudgetPlanner, FingerprintLeaseCoordinator, ResumeContractVerifier` from cross-area-facades, and includes the \"A6 performance budgets\" describe using `planner.replanOnResume(...)`, `planner.resumeReexecutions`, `coordinator.coordinatePause`, `verifier.verify`. So the performance-budge