2c (which is what the frozen tests were written against). Actually wait — the frozen performance-budgets at digest 4502f116 matches _a01verify (LF-normalized). And _a01verify has cross-area-facades.ts + that performance-budgets + all the guard tests. So _a01verify IS essentially the \"expected verified final state\" for this task (someone already ran a similar trial for a01 and it contains this task's target files!).\n\nHmm, _a01verify seems to be a workspace where an agent (doing a different task, A01) also created these files. Actually no — more likely _a01verify is a \"verification\" workspace for a01 that happened to have the candidate tree 96afc2c... Wait, but 96afc2c is the trial base commit for these RSI tasks (the \"candidate\" in manifest source). Yes! manifest.source.candidate.commit = 96afc2c. And the trial base directories are git-archive of... hmm.\n\nActually the key realization: `_a01verify/ClawX` = the reference/verification workspace which corresponds to candidate 96afc2c PLUS the a01 task solution. And it contains cross-area-facades.ts etc. because 96afc2c itself contains them (cand column showed present).\n\nWait no — cand=96afc2c HAS cross-area-facades.ts (b521ddca). And the trial `base` dirs are derived from baseCommit. The agent workspace is missing the files because... hmm, actually the agent workspace should be identical to base. But base also lacks cross-area-facades.ts? Let me re-check: my earlier comparison showed base lacks cross-area-facades.ts too. Let me verify what baseCommit fd04f0b contains.\n\nFrom the comparison: fd04f0b (base) → cross-area-facades ABSENT. 96afc2c (candidate) → present. So the workspace base is fd04f0b (no facade), and the RSI task expects the agent to recreate it.\n\nBut hold on — the *trial* `base` directory in the run is presumably also fd04f0b. And in the trial, the agent = current workspace (fd04f0b + nothing). So I need to add the facade.\n\nNow, importantly: the frozen `performance-budgets.test.ts` (oracle)