cks that do not install dependencies, and return the required structured result.\" And RESULT_SCHEMA requires status/summary/testsRun.\n\nSo my deliverable: implement the change (create the files), run checks (vitest), and return the structured JSON.\n\nBut there's a critical constraint: I cannot install deps and there's no node_modules in the workspace. So I can't run vitest in the workspace... unless I use the node_modules from _a01verify. Hmm, but that's a different workspace. Actually _a01verify/ClawX has node_modules AND openclaw_runtime/node_modules etc. \n\nWait — is _a01verify/ClawX actually a full checkout equivalent to the trial base? It has node_modules. Let me check whether it's git-linked. There's `_cmp.cjs` referencing worktrees. Let me look more carefully: maybe _a01verify/ClawX is a junction/symlink to the same worktree.\n\nLet me check if _a01verify/ClawX is a real dir or a link, and compare its files to the agent workspace.\n\nActually, the simplest robust approach: \n1. Create the needed files in the agent workspace.\n2. Run the oracle commands using a node_modules that exists.\n\nSince the trial harness's oracle command is `pnpm exec vitest run ...` run inside the workspace, and the workspace has no node_modules, presumably the harness supplies node_modules (nodeModulesPath in manifest = C:\\Users\\27933\\.codex\\worktrees\\tf0604-rsi-baseline\\ClawX\\node_modules). Let me check if that path exists.\n\nIt said True earlier for `Test-Path 'C:\\Users\\27933\\.codex\\worktrees\\tf0604-rsi-baseline\\ClawX\\node_modules'`. So the harness mounts node_modules there, likely via a junction into the workspace at grading time, or via NODE_PATH.\n\nFor me to run tests locally, I can create a junction from the trial agent dir to that node_modules. But \"do not install dependencies\" — using an existing node_modules is fine (not installing).\n\nHmm, but actually maybe the workspace already resolves node_modules via a pnpm workspace setup. Let me check the agen